{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed","id":523042,"title":"Feed limitation legally imposed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-21T02:31:30-07:00","id":523042,"title":"Feed limitation legally imposed","content":"I was working on using my city, Triest (Italy) as the setting of a vampire campaign and I'd like to hear some advice.<br /> <br /> One of the concepts I came out is a feed limitation: by decree of the Invictus the Kindreds are divided in two parts: the full citizens and the Young Bloods who are forbidden to drink human blood and have minor civil and political rights.<br /> <br /> This disctintion was imposed to defend the Masquerade, due also to the high numbers of vampires in the city and the spreading of videorecording tools. It forces the Young Bloods to feed from animals like boars and dears which they hunt at the limit of the city [in the real Triest there are many of them nearby the city]. <br /> <br /> Nowadays the maximum number of full citizens is set and won't go higher. This leads to a harsh competions between YBs looking for a promotion; a battle of the have-nots which makes them willing to do anything in order to gain their space in society. Quite often YBs are used by the elders because the formers hope to gain the favours of the latters.<br /> <br /> This really helps the mantaining of the status quo. In fact Young Bloods due to low BP have very small access to vampiric powers and are easily terrified by the sight of the more powerful ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6012-jute","name":"Jute","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T03:08:06-07:00","id":523064,"title":"","content":"I think this would potentially cause more masquerade breaches than it prevents. Vamp hits blood potency 3 -&gt; cant eat animals any more without spending willpower -&gt; more likely to be hungry/starving -&gt; Frenzy time. <br /> <br /> A shit about city laws, the Beast giveth not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T04:37:12-07:00","id":523087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523064#post523064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this would potentially cause more masquerade breaches than it prevents. Vamp hits blood potency 3 -&gt; cant eat animals any more without spending willpower -&gt; more likely to be hungry/starving -&gt; Frenzy time.<br /> <br /> A shit about city laws, the Beast giveth not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I don't think that it would be a common ocurance. Such person should have the time to get the promotion? Unless of course his blood thickens extra fast, then he's boned. <br /> <br /> But all in all, I'm also against such an idea, mostly because vamps need a lot more animal blood than they need from humans. If you had a sizeable population of vamps feeding only on animals, they would probably go extinct quite fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:17:43-07:00","id":523117,"title":"","content":"How many vampires are you talking about in this scenario? And are full citizens allowed to award feeding from humans as a temporary privilege? And regardless of whether or not the answer yes, if this is one where all the covenants exist it's not likely to be enforceable. A starving population of vampires with nothing to lose is a much larger potential Masquerade breach and threat to the status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T06:32:54-07:00","id":523128,"title":"","content":"I kind of like the idea of a locked blood-economy. Perhaps with a ration to keep destruction of the animal population in check. Designated centers where you go for appointed, official feedings. <br /> <br /> It'd be a very different kind of game where vitae is a very precious resource, so you have to be careful when you want to go in hard and risk a bunch of blood that you can't legally replenish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:09:07-07:00","id":523142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523128#post523128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of like the idea of a locked blood-economy. Perhaps with a ration to keep destruction of the animal population in check. Designated centers where you go for appointed, official feedings.<br /> <br /> It'd be a very different kind of game where vitae is a very precious resource, so you have to be careful when you want to go in hard and risk a bunch of blood that you can't legally replenish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am with Smarmy on this. The concept seems unique and interesting, but I do see some potential issues. The animal population would be in danger. With a human, you want to keep it alive because of the consequences of becoming a serial killer, who cares if you murder a deer every night, It's just a deer... (some neonates would think this) Then if they are filling up on an animal every night where the elders have rationed off humans it makes it a little more... iffy.<br /> <br /> Also I think it might cause a lot more neonates to have powers that dont require vitae to use. That doesn't necessarily make them weaker. A vamp with 5 vigor or celerity Doesnt -have to- use vitae the benefits are still great without it. even better with just a little bit of vitae. Mesmerize, Faces in the crowd.<br /> <br /> Next... Ghouls and blood dolls? Outlawed then too? A lot of vamps would want to attach themselves to a human they could call their own if blood was scarce... It would make some merits completely useless ( herd )<br /> <br /> My next question... What would keep the young Kindred, who know what the world is like today, from just... moving? I know I wouldnt want to starve or eat animals if I could just hop a plane to say... anywhere else.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to be harsh, just giving you some food for thought ^_^<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:21:39-07:00","id":523149,"title":"","content":"Honestly I would expect every have-not to band together, join the Carthian movement and collectively tell the Invictus precisely where they can shove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:52:02-07:00","id":523188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523149#post523149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I would expect every have-not to band together, join the Carthian movement and collectively tell the Invictus precisely where they can shove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So everyone have-not in real life goes and forms a labor union or separatist enclave? Because that expectation is about equivalent to that.<br /> <br /> Although admittedly, you are working with a much smaller group when it comes to local vampires compared to local humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:53:11-07:00","id":523191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523149#post523149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I would expect every have-not to band together, join the Carthian movement and collectively tell the Invictus precisely where they can shove it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You would probably expect similar things of slaves, etc. Great struggles where needed for them to become free, even while outnumbering their superiors. In this case, these superiors are also much stronger then you are. So I don't say it's <i>that</i> easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:54:00-07:00","id":523195,"title":"","content":"Sounds like perfect fodder for a decent-sized chronicle arc to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T07:59:08-07:00","id":523247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523087#post523087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I don't think that it would be a common ocurance. Such person should have the time to get the promotion? Unless of course his blood thickens extra fast, then he's boned.<br /> <br /> But all in all, I'm also against such an idea, mostly because vamps need a lot more animal blood than they need from humans. If you had a sizeable population of vamps feeding only on animals, they would probably go extinct quite fast.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Vamps take over all the slaughter houses in and near the city. The amount of animals that get slaughtered in the US per year is more than enough to feed all the BP 1-2 Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:13:03-07:00","id":523261,"title":"","content":"In real life the have-nots don't slowly grow in power and the need to violate the law as they age. And aren't generally more functional during the day than their oppressors. And since the only way up is via the Klingon method what motive do the unwashed masses have to <i>not</i> firebomb Citizens in their sleep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:19:28-07:00","id":523266,"title":"","content":"Does this city have a slaughter house?<br /> <br /> I think, since the world is a little different than the time of slaves ( in the US anyway ) that the neonates would have an easier time banding together than forming a smaller movement and yes often small groups rebel. Good plot for a story. I do think that this would not be a sustainable effort in today's world. I agree with Elfive here, why wouldnt they rebel asap? They would be young and still cling to human thoughts, and everyone desires to be free.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:29:22-07:00","id":523276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523261#post523261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And aren't generally more functional during the day than their oppressors.</div> </div> </div> </div> Low BP/High Humanity vampires are better at not burning than High BP/Low Humanity Vampires, but remaining active in the daytime requires a Stamina + Resolve (+ Resilience) roll, which arguably tends to favour the elders, especially Ventrue and Gangrel who will have had more time to increase their Stamina, Resolve and Resilience.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T08:38:22-07:00","id":523300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523276#post523276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Low BP/High Humanity vampires are better at not burning than High BP/Low Humanity Vampires, but remaining active in the daytime requires a Stamina + Resolve (+ Resilience) roll, which arguably tends to favour the elders, especially Ventrue and Gangrel who will have had more time to increase their Stamina, Resolve and Resilience.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they might have more human connections left from their former life. Elders tend to have a harder time with humans due to lower humanity. I guess there is probably a counter to every argument in play here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:15:11-07:00","id":523329,"title":"","content":"Um. Maybe I'm missing something, but I feel like there's a fairly obvious issue that isn't being addressed. A neonate needs either Animal Ken (fairly high levels for wild animals like boars, in my opinion), animalism, or the ability to grapple and drain a boar or deer (each of which requiring different super-human abilities) to be able to regularly feed from boars and deer. This is not a matter of human-style hunting. If you kill the animal, it's useless. Even with a spear keeping it at bay, hunting injuries to boar are exceedingly common. Since you need vitae to heal, it's a losing proposition.<br /> <br /> Blood that isn't fresh is near-useless, too, if we're talking about 2e. That means you pretty much have to feed from a living animal. That means slaughterhouses aren't really an option like they are in Buffy (and maybe older versions of Vampire; I can't claim familiarity.) At least not to feed an entire city's neonates with.<br /> <br /> So unless you're buying a few kittens a day (a masquerade risk in its own right) or specifically geared for it or going after livestock (another masquerade risk), I don't think feeding from animals is really feasible. It works for some Kindred (those already inclined towards it, like Gangrel), but I can't imagine all Neonates being relegated to it and surviving for more than a couple weeks.<br /> <br /> I also find the idea of restricted feeding interesting, but I don't think animals-only for an entire class of vampire is the way to go for the reasons above. I'd suggest something closer to quotas, but I really have no idea how you could police that. Really, no idea how you could enforce animals-only. You'd probably just get a massive amount of unregulated &quot;poachers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, now I'm getting a whole &quot;drug war&quot; or &quot;prohibition&quot; vibe, which may be totally fun to play with if that's where you want to go with it. Neonates selling and trading blood dolls on the vampiric black market. Sneaking bites when and where they think no citizen-ranked vampires are looking. Could be fun.<br /> <br /> Really, I think given human (ha) and vampire nature, you'd get less vying for promotion if it's as locked down as you say. Instead you'd have a thriving blood market. Maybe even run by some of the &quot;citizens&quot; for favors and resources under the radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:24:52-07:00","id":523338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523300#post523300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they might have more human connections left from their former life.</div> </div> </div> </div> So? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523300#post523300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Elders tend to have a harder time with humans due to lower humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> They have a harder time with healthy relationships, that doesn't mean they don't have armies of ghouls and other mortal servants.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:43:42-07:00","id":523393,"title":"","content":"Does cold animal blood work any different to cold human blood? Because at a minimum cold blood gets you a vitae every 2 pints, and humans have roughly 8-10 pints of blood, so a human-sized animal would have a similar quantity and yield about 4 or 5 vitae for someone of blood potency 1. Which is actually more than the book says you get from it while it's alive. Now, that may need fixing but the point is that there's not a massive net loss for the lower end who can actually drink the stuff easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:47:31-07:00","id":523396,"title":"","content":"Black market blood trade. <br /> <br /> Smugglers/coyotes. <br /> <br /> Roaming blood doll dens. <br /> <br /> Favors paid in literal blood. <br /> <br /> Underground cells working to bring down the upper echelon within their own covenant. Neonates are neonates. <br /> <br /> Doing horrible dirty work for meager, but extra, blood rations. <br /> <br /> There are so many seeds here I'm gonna start digging furrows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:54:26-07:00","id":523400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523393#post523393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does cold animal blood work any different to cold human blood? Because at a minimum cold blood gets you a vitae every 2 pints, and humans have roughly 8-10 pints of blood, so a human-sized animal would have a similar quantity and yield about 4 or 5 vitae for someone of blood potency 1. Which is actually more than the book says you get from it while it's alive. Now, that may need fixing but the point is that there's not a massive net loss for the lower end who can actually drink the stuff easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not aware of the book explicitly mentioning one way or the other, but given that animal blood comes after cold blood in the text, I would personally rule that they are separate. Animal blood is markedly less potent than human blood. That's in the book. Cold human blood doesn't last more than a night, and it gives far less than fresh. That's also in the book. Given all of that, I'd have slaughterhouse blood give nothing at all. Of course, with how vague the book is, I'm sure another ST could have a different interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:01:53-07:00","id":523433,"title":"","content":"My assumption was that fundamentally, blood is blood. Being in a human gives it a leg up on the turn-into-vitae train, being in another species gives it less of one. Take it out of either and it drops down to pretty much the same level. Note how taking vitae out of a vampire makes it quickly drop to cold blood <i>regardless of the original source.</i> That implies that the <i>vessel</i> is the important bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:15:25-07:00","id":523447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523329#post523329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Blood that isn't fresh is near-useless, too, if we're talking about 2e. That means you pretty much have to feed from a living animal.</div> </div> </div> </div> And? Why can't the vampire's suck them dry? That would make the meat Kosher/Halal! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523329#post523329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> going after livestock (another masquerade risk),</div> </div> </div> </div> Why would a slaughterhouse be a masquerade risk? I would assume the vampires would buy and take over the slaughterhouse before feeding there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:19:11-07:00","id":523451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523433#post523433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My assumption was that fundamentally, blood is blood. Being in a human gives it a leg up on the turn-into-vitae train, being in another species gives it less of one. Take it out of either and it drops down to pretty much the same level. Note how taking vitae out of a vampire makes it quickly drop to cold blood <i>regardless of the original source.</i> That implies that the <i>vessel</i> is the important bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, given that they specify for Kindred vitae and don't for animal, I'd personally take that as further evidence that cold blood from animals is worthless. Once again, it's a matter of interpretation with no explicit explanation in the book. The description of what Vitae (About Vitae, pg 98) is versus mundane blood, however, indicates to me that Vitae is Vitae, not so much Blood is Blood. Animals produce less usable Vitae, but once it is Vitae, it's all the same.<br /> <br /> Blood Supplies on page 95 especially indicates to me that the raw material that makes Vitae is something within blood, not the blood itself, and one could infer from the rest of the text that humans have more of it, and it degrades rapidly without life to sustain it or a vampire's body to maintain it.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'll reiterate that I'm just going with the evidence I've found, and YMMV. Not saying your perspective is wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:22:12-07:00","id":523452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523451#post523451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, given that they specify for Kindred vitae and don't for animal, I'd personally take that as further evidence that cold blood from animals is worthless.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, but why do you keep assuming <i>cold</i> blood? I've already stated the assumption for slaughterhouses is that you drain the <i>living</i> animals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T10:35:20-07:00","id":523465,"title":"","content":"I brought up cold blood in relation to killing an animal and <i>then</i> draining it vs draining it while it was alive, because the former (if viable, which was the subject of the debate) would be easier for neonates to pull off. <br /> <br /> That said, I've since realised since posting that my interpretation does have the notable flaw of allowing Kindred to flout the feeding limitations without spending willpower by virtue of sheer quantity. Then I pictured an elder feeding by draining an entire herd of cows and decided I liked it, so now I'm keeping it anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:33:41-07:00","id":523518,"title":"","content":"I wonder how something like that would be enforced. And it really seems like a city verging on a particularly bloody rebellion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T11:36:40-07:00","id":523521,"title":"","content":"Lucrative feeding grounds protected/watched, and extremely harsh punishments for violations they discover. Of course there could be plenty of illegal feeding, but the whole point is to establish serious fear of trying it. <br /> <br /> A specialized oath, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:32:21-07:00","id":523573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523465#post523465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I brought up cold blood in relation to killing an animal and <i>then</i> draining it vs draining it while it was alive, because the former (if viable, which was the subject of the debate) would be easier for neonates to pull off.</div> </div> </div> </div> If Jewish and Muslim butchers can kill cattle by draining their blood, I'm sure neonates can manage it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523465#post523465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I've since realised since posting that my interpretation does have the notable flaw of allowing Kindred to flout the feeding limitations without spending willpower by virtue of sheer quantity. Then I pictured an elder feeding by draining an entire herd of cows and decided I liked it, so now I'm keeping it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>An elder would have difficulty spending enough willpower to drain a herd of cattle, unless your doing away with the rule about spending willpower.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:33:59-07:00","id":523574,"title":"","content":"Animals would still be subject to the Kiss. So if you can manage to bite them non-violently, they Swoon(ing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:45:17-07:00","id":523587,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?193415-V-tR-Old-MacDracul-had-a-farm-Ee-I-Ee-I-O\" target=\"_blank\">Many of these arguments were raised a decade ago.</a> Though that was for 1st Ed Requiem, the rules have changed some what since then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T12:48:29-07:00","id":523590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523338#post523338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So?<br /> <br /> They have a harder time with healthy relationships, that doesn't mean they don't have armies of ghouls and other mortal servants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And to your &quot;So?&quot; as well I was referencing an earlier post on how difficult it would be to have a neonate vs elder to fight during the day and throw around fire. I think a neonate would have more connections to their human lives and have an easier time convincing ( Non supernaturally ) humans to help them.<br /> <br /> Again the ghoul army .... that would require a lot of vitae to maintain which is .... what we are debating about Blood is hard to come by,... Are ghouls even legal... if you cant easily get vitae.. would you want to be dishing it out to your ghouls? They cant even feed to replenish themselves, you'd have to do it for them should they want to use their vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:11:02-07:00","id":523626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523590#post523590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And to your &quot;So?&quot; as well I was referencing an earlier post on how difficult it would be to have a neonate vs elder to fight during the day and throw around fire. I think a neonate would have more connections to their human lives and have an easier time convincing ( Non supernaturally ) humans to help them.</div> </div> </div> </div> And? Elders can <i>supernaturally</i> convince people to help them.<br /> <br /> 5 levels of Majesty will give you +5 dice to your Presence rolls, negates all penalties to Social rolls, and allows you to inflict the Charmed condition on people, all for 0 vitae.<br /> <br /> Mesmerize, Entombed Command and Conditioning are all 0 vitae, as is Iron Edict if the victim is in a Vinculum with the vampire.<br /> <br /> And elders have had the time to buy up their social attributes and skills to higher levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523590#post523590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again the ghoul army .... that would require a lot of vitae to maintain which is .... what we are debating about Blood is hard to come by,... Are ghouls even legal... if you cant easily get vitae.. would you want to be dishing it out to your ghouls? They cant even feed to replenish themselves, you'd have to do it for them should they want to use their vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div> Let's look at the numbers shall we? <br /> <br /> A ghoul requires 1 vitae per month minimum.<br /> <br /> 1 vitae costs 1 lethal health level.<br /> <br /> Lethal: One point is regained in two days.<br /> <br /> In 30 days 15 points of lethal damage are healed.<br /> <br /> Therefore a ghoul can more than pay for it's own upkeep in vitae.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T13:14:55-07:00","id":523653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523573#post523573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An elder would have difficulty spending enough willpower to drain a herd of cattle, unless your doing away with the rule about spending willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even at blood potency 5 it would take 150 pints of cold blood to fill up. That's a fair few cows. Then I thought, hey, if that much counted as a meal in a vat, why do you need to bother taking it out of the cow? <br /> <br /> Then that morphed into this idea for a houserule that says &quot;Without willpower expenditure, anything below your feeding restriction counts as cold blood, and any vampire can get nourishment from this by drinking BP x 2 pints&quot; so like at blood potency 7 you could get a single vitae by either doing a human 1 lethal and paying a willpower, or by <i>completely draining two people dry</i>. Because I feel this game is lacking a &quot;mountain of corpses&quot; feeding option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:55:15-07:00","id":523724,"title":"","content":"While they do have some stud farms it doesn't exactly look like cattle country. The place is on a hill that leads up to a mountain, and is more of a seaport trading center. That's just from some looking around wikipedia but even Jute said there's deer and boars and didn't suggest huge amounts of cattle.<br /> <br /> Can you get Vitae from fish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T14:58:29-07:00","id":523727,"title":"","content":"I imagine it'd follow the normal animal rules. So it's going to take a <i>hell</i> of a lot of sardines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:09:16-07:00","id":523731,"title":"","content":"I'd say anything that uses haemoglobin is ok, but shellfish like crabs are no good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T15:35:07-07:00","id":523763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523724#post523724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While they do have some stud farms it doesn't exactly look like cattle country. The place is on a hill that leads up to a mountain, and is more of a seaport trading center. That's just from some looking around wikipedia but even Jute said there's deer and boars and didn't suggest huge amounts of cattle.<br /> <br /> Can you get Vitae from fish?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like sheep or goat country. Wikipedia says the population is around <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">205,535 which suggests 2 to 20 vampires. If we assume there are 20 and half of those are BP 1-2 that's only 10 vampires to feed with animals.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":299,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","user":"NineDaysDead","date":". 05-21-2015, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T19:13:22-07:00","id":523840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523447#post523447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And? Why can't the vampire's suck them dry? That would make the meat Kosher/Halal!</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I spent the majority of my post explaining how difficult it is to feed from living wild animals. Dead cattle cause investigations, so it's not really wise to be draining livestock dry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523447#post523447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would a slaughterhouse be a masquerade risk? I would assume the vampires would buy and take over the slaughterhouse before feeding there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall saying it would be, though I don't know how many vampires a single slaughterhouse can support. Everything I've seen posted show national numbers, which are useless for these purposes. I really can't fathom every neonate in a city either owning or being employed by a vampire-owned slaughterhouse. That's remarkably improbable and stretches masquerade. I suppose it's possible, though. If a vampire owned a slaughterhouse, they could feed from their own stock worry-free, sure. I just don't think owning a slaughterhouse is any more realistic an expectation for neonates than going out and hunting wild animals to drink.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NineDaysDead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523452#post523452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, but why do you keep assuming <i>cold</i> blood? I've already stated the assumption for slaughterhouses is that you drain the <i>living</i> animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went back and re-read all your posts. As near as I could find, you did not specify living animals. But as for living animals, I suppose if a vampire owns cattle, they can safely feed from that cattle all they like. Still doesn't explain how you get every non-Citizen vampire in a city to own their own cattle, either in a ranch or a slaughterhouse. I live in a city of 100,000 that's pretty much defined by its cattle industry (seriously, we're nicknamed Cow Town in local news, and you can smell the stench of either cow or meat processing over the entire city when the wind blows right), and we still only have one slaughterhouse. I doubt you'd have many more in a big city that doesn't have the land for ranches to raise their own cattle.<br /> <br /> In the interest of completeness, I looked up some statistics of my local slaughterhouse.<br /> <br /> It processes up to 5,500 cattle per day. Frankly, this was a somewhat life-changing number to learn. Took a while to wrap my head around the scale. Therefore, even if each cow only produced one Vitae, I will admit that this is easily enough to feed all the vampires in a city.<br /> <br /> The downside being: it also employs 5,000 individuals. You run into a whole new issue of keeping the feeding secret from that many people. If you're employing Kindred, you have to worry about the fatal and near-fatal heavy machinery accidents that happen there often enough that there's a real risk of someone witnessing a Kindred getting hurt during a night shift or whatever. You'd have to figure out how you handle that. Whether they can come back, perfectly fine, after such an injury without raising questions. Additionally, these cattle are shipped in via semi-truck all throughout the day. They aren't really stored there. There's not enough space, and the ranches here don't produce nearly 5,500 cattle per day. Pretty sure they're shipped in from elsewhere, which means you probably don't even have living animals there during the hours vampires are awake.<br /> <br /> Granted, this is just my experience and knowledge from my own local plant, which is one of the larger ones in the world I believe. I don't really have the stomach to research the field too heavily. Already had to disable images on my browser to research this much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:33:33-07:00","id":523935,"title":"","content":"There is one solution to this that hasn't been approached. Young Bloods aren't able to feed off of Humans. That doesn't mean that they can not feed off of Full Citizen Kindred that can feed off of Humans. They risk Blood Bond, but that could be a way that the Elders try to control the neonates. &quot;You can't feed off of animals anymore? Well, you can feed from me and be my obedient servant.&quot; Heck, one of the Antagonists books have a Ventrue that does this, making everybody think he is a pathetic loser as they try to Bind him, whereas he is already Bound to someone who is in torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1840-akashicmonk","name":"akashicmonk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1840_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T10:32:53-07:00","id":524568,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your great feedback!<br /> <br /> My idea was about a city with a population of 200'000 with more or less 20-30 vampires.<br /> Following the ratio -which of course is just an advice and blah blah blah- they should be only 4.<br /> This justifies in my opinion a strong attention to the Masquerade also due to the presence of a group of hunters in the city (Malleus Malleficarum probably).<br /> <br /> I still haven't decided how many of the vampires should be Young Bloods; I'm juggling between 5 and 15 (plus the neonate players); it strongly depends on how long is this period in a life of a Kindred. I could choose to use it just as an evaluation period which goes on for most for around a year; or I could settle it to be longer like a decade or two being a very strong division in the kindred society.<br /> This second option would be much more interesting for me but it would also be more difficult to make it work plausibly as you noted.<br /> <br /> Anyway I've a few answers which I thought before or thanks to you:<br /> <br /> -there should be a market for the ones who can't hunt and in order to mantain the animal popolation. This would be both legally, an Invictus livestock, and illegally, smugglers of animal and human blood.<br /> This livestock would be a normal livestock owned by a vampire which sells meat to the humans but during the night is guarded only by a few ghouls who let vampires feed in exchange of favors to their sire or sometimes money or YBs' vitae.<br /> <br /> -the punishment for a Kindred found feeding from humans should be very harsh; maybe even final death or torture.<br /> <br /> -there is a strong cultural imposition: imagine yourselves entering in the kindred society after the embrace without a clue of what you should do and being taught that this is how you should behave and that you've to resist the urge of drinking human blood because you're not ready yet.<br /> <br /> -the Carthian movement, which was almost non existent before this law, could gain great influence which could also slowly lead to a revolt in the long run if the rule is not changed but in order to do so it first should pacify the YBs.<br /> --&gt;to make this choice more interesting if the law is removed there will be more hunters in the story<br /> <br /> -some YBs in order to get the promotion can choose to show their total fidelity to the Prince getting a vinculum to him and making his power more stable.<br /> <br /> <br /> This leaves me with a few problems:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/523042-feed-limitation-legally-imposed?p=523142#post523142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls and blood dolls? Outlawed then too? A lot of vamps would want to attach themselves to a human they could call their own if blood was scarce... It would make some merits completely useless ( herd )<br /> <br /> My next question... What would keep the young Kindred, who know what the world is like today, from just... moving? I know I wouldnt want to starve or eat animals if I could just hop a plane to say... anywhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>About the merits I think you're right. And yes, ghouls and blood dolls would be outlawed. Maybe I shouldn't let players take them at the beginning. Anyway with their characters and their knowledge of this city growing they could take them but at their own risk which would probably be being blackmailed by someone if they are not good enough to keep a secret.<br /> <br /> About them going away the only answers I have for now are big dangers around this city (werewolves, cities which doesn't answer anymore probably because of something tragic) and the lack of contacts.<br /> In fact due to the over population of Kindreds, new ones can be embraced only with a specific permission of the Prince who use this power to gain favours from the elders. This means that neonates are created only when their sire really wants it which makes the latters very useful contacts for the formers in their early stages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6012-jute","name":"Jute","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T06:55:29-07:00","id":527626,"title":"","content":"There is a certain amount of suspension of disbelief available when running a game, so I wouldn't worry about ratios. I would focus less on feasibility and more on &quot;what stories does this idea allow me to tell?&quot;<br /> <br /> If the player go all &quot;WTF. There would be a rebellion&quot; then stroke your chin, hrm loudly, nod, and say &quot;Yes. You should get on that.&quot;<br /> <br /> In terms of Framing, I'd have The Primogen, a council of 5 Elders that have the for realzies power. Then I'd have ~25 of the &quot;Haves&quot; with a &quot;Prince&quot; chosen from their ranks that is <i>technically </i>in charge. Then have some number of the &quot;Have Nots&quot; (anywhere from 50 to 125). I would also note that strict feeding rules are probably meant to address the overpopulation problem as much as the &quot;Malleus Malefcarum is in our back yard&quot; problem.<br /> <br /> Nearby slaughterhouses or owned animals become excellent examples of the Herd merit and prime real-estate for elders to own and rent out. As do animal shelters and other facilities that collect stray animals.<br /> <br /> I would allow the &quot;Haves&quot; to temporarily extend feeding rights to the have nots. Make this an affair if it comes up. Maybe dope the mortal up on some narcotics to make it feel even better. When you get to this scene, it's going to do a <i>lot </i>to set the tone of your game, so you want to do it right.<br /> <br /> I would allow the &quot;Have nots&quot; to be allowed to feed from vampires freely, especially each other.<br /> <br /> In terms of enforcing... turning in your peer gets you feeding rights for a month. I mean if you want it to be hard enforcement, just use Oaths, but I'd recommend against it. Underground and black-market mortal trading can definately be a thing.<br /> <br /> You really want to decide how you want to handle Ghouls, since it's a work around. Ultimately a 2-3 Ghouls can keep a Vampire running at minimum fed indefinitely, until something goes wrong. I'd make a really huge deal to be allowed to make one, and having a Ghoul being a huge status symbol (probably Have or &quot;just about to be a Have&quot; or &quot;Performed some legendary service&quot; only.)<br /> <br /> A key to &quot;soft&quot; enforcement, which is what I'd recommend, is detection. Have Mekhet be the prominent enforcers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 05-25-2015, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}